<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Java War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1825">1825</a>–<a href="/years/1830">1830</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Diponegoro War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> War was a rebellion in central Java from 1825 to 1830 led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diponegoro">Prince Diponegoro</a> of Yogyakarta against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colonial rule and the Javanese courts that cooperated with it. Fuelled by peasant grievances, Islamic sentiment and Dutch interference, it was fought as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war. Diponegoro was captured during negotiations in 1830 and exiled. About 200,000 Javanese died, and the costs led the Dutch to introduce the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultivation-system">Cultivation System</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/java-war.jpg" alt="Java War" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: J.P. van de Veer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bestorming_van_Pleret.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
